      "cooked": "<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/7/8/78f14dee66b80fb3c7672341fda6284affb55000.png\" data-download-href=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/78f14dee66b80fb3c7672341fda6284affb55000\" title=\"erpnext_list_settings\"><img src=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/7/8/78f14dee66b80fb3c7672341fda6284affb55000_2_690x162.png\" alt=\"erpnext_list_settings\" data-base62-sha1=\"hfUhU64jTbAwyMGNvWLGvwNT0g8\" width=\"690\" height=\"162\" srcset=\"https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/7/8/78f14dee66b80fb3c7672341fda6284affb55000_2_690x162.png, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/optimized/3X/7/8/78f14dee66b80fb3c7672341fda6284affb55000_2_1035x243.png 1.5x, https://discuss.frappe.io/uploads/default/original/3X/7/8/78f14dee66b80fb3c7672341fda6284affb55000.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"F3F3F7\"><div class=\"meta\"><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">erpnext_list_settings</span><span class=\"informations\">1063×251 27.7 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg></div></a></div></p>\n<p>Greetings Everyone!</p>\n<p>I have had difficulty adding permissions to other Roles to use the List Settings. In this case, I am wanting to give the Report Manager the ability to add or remove columns to any list view. Here is what I have tried so far:</p>\n<p>-I added List View Settings for the Report Manager in the Roles Permissions Manager<br>\n-I inserted the Report Manager Role into the Doctype “List View Settings” by adding Report Manager into the script files<br>\n-I have cleared cache, migrated the site, and restarted the server for erpnext to see the changes, but it has not implemented them</p>\n<p>any help would be appreciated and I will try to followup with any information I can, that could assist in solving this problem, thank you all!</p>",
